# Full-Ewald counterpart of in.gcpm: pair gcpm/long + kspace pppm/dipole.
#
# Same GCPM water model and data file as in.gcpm, but the long-range
# electrostatics (charge-charge, charge-dipole, dipole-dipole) are treated
# with the full Ewald/PPPM method instead of the per-pair reaction field:
#   - pair_style gcpm/long with eps_rf = 0 (RF is not supported here)
#   - kspace_style pppm/dipole
#   - NO neigh_modify exclude: the intramolecular Coulomb exclusion is done
#     internally by molecule ID, so the real-space subtraction cancels the
#     k-space contributions of excluded pairs exactly.
#
# Expectations vs in.gcpm (RF, eps 78.4): reaction field and Ewald are
# different long-range treatments of the same model, so the absolute
# potential energy carries a systematic offset (RF vs tinfoil-Ewald
# bookkeeping); temperature/pressure distributions and energy fluctuations
# should agree within statistical error for homogeneous water.

variable equil_steps     index 1000
variable relax_steps     index 1000
variable datafile  index data.gcpm
variable r         index 1

variable T         index 298
variable P         index 1.0         # 1 atm = 0.101 MPa

variable velseed   index 817324
variable seed      index 576211

# cutoff must equal the Fortran rcut printed at startup (e.g. 11.220684 Ang)
variable rc        index 11.220684

units real
atom_style hybrid full dipole sphere
